== Checked result
For characteristic-$p$ coefficient rings and $q = p^e$, the named Lean theorem proves that $g^q$ and the coefficientwise $q$-Frobenius twist of $g$ agree modulo the ideal generated by $x_i^q - x_i$. The producer's field/prime assumptions are instances of this Lean statement. A blind algebraic derivation and an independent Lean/source inspection agree at this scope.

